   "text": "Once upon a time, there was a little boy named Leo who loved to explore the world. He was curious, brave, and always eager to try new things. One sunny morning, he found himself standing at the edge of the sidewalk, looking at the bike in front of him.\n\nBicycle was heavy, but Leo felt the pull of adventure. He took a deep breath and stepped forward. The bike moved forward, slow at first, but he kept going. He watched other kids ride, some with confidence, some with fear. He felt a little bit of fear too. Leo tried again, pushing harder, and the bike moved a little faster. He looked down at his feet and felt the pedals. He felt the wind in his hair. He was moving, and he was learning.\n\nFrom that day on, Leo was always eager to learn. He practiced every day, and soon he was able to ride on his own. He learned to balance, to steer, to stop. He was no longer just a boy who wanted to try. He was a rider. And so, with determination and joy, they mastered the journey on two wheels.",
